Subject: [PATCH] Fix dtype mismatch on 32-bit systems

In BlockManager._rebuild_blknos_and_blklocs, the length (shape[0]) might be 
treated as a 64-bit integer, while the pre-allocated new_blknos and new_blklocs
arrays expect intp_t (32-bit on ARM). 

Force the dtype to be intp specifically.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]
Signed-off-by: Gemini CLI <gemini-cli@google.com>

--- a/pandas/_libs/internals.pyx
+++ b/pandas/_libs/internals.pyx
@@ -746,7 +746,7 @@
         """
         cdef:
             intp_t blkno, i, j
-            cnp.npy_intp length = self.shape[0]
+            cnp.npy_intp length = <cnp.npy_intp>self.shape[0]
             SharedBlock blk
             BlockPlacement bp
             ndarray[intp_t, ndim=1] new_blknos, new_blklocs
